From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: World of Warcraft <warcraft@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 06:17:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] fmt: no compile-time format string checks

fmt 10.2.1's consteval format strings aren't constant expressions to clang 20 (FMT_STRING in
format-inl.h, os.cc), which refuses them. Its own switch, FMT_CONSTEVAL, set empty for it and
everything using it.
---
 dep/fmt/CMakeLists.txt | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dep/fmt/CMakeLists.txt b/dep/fmt/CMakeLists.txt
index fc9b1f7..93d9bb0 100644
--- a/dep/fmt/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/dep/fmt/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -33,6 +33,12 @@ target_include_directories(fmt
   PUBLIC
     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include)
 
+# Format strings checked as the program runs, not as it compiles: this fmt (10.2.1)'s compile-time
+# check isn't a constant expression to newer clang (20), which then refuses it.
+target_compile_definitions(fmt
+  PUBLIC
+    FMT_CONSTEVAL=)
+
 target_link_libraries(fmt
   PRIVATE
     trinity-dependency-interface)
